# CinemaVault Next — client-side environment (Vite exposes VITE_* to the browser).
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real values; .env* is git-ignored (except this file).
#
# Use a DEVELOPMENT or PREVIEW Supabase project for local work — not the production project.

# Supabase project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase *publishable* (anon) key. This key is designed to be public; Row Level Security protects data.
# NEVER put the service-role / secret key here: anything prefixed VITE_ ships to every visitor's browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# development | preview | production
VITE_APP_ENV=development
# supabase | mock. Leave unset for Supabase. `mock` shows sample data and is refused when VITE_APP_ENV=production.
# On the dev server with no Supabase variables at all, sample data is used automatically; a half-configured
# or production build never falls back to it.
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=

# Server-only (Vercel function, NOT prefixed with VITE_): TMDB_API_KEY — set in the Vercel dashboard, never here.
